{
  "title": "RamekinAPI repeats guard/URL/Bearer/parseError boilerplate in \
every method",
  "description": "Each endpoint in `Shared/RamekinAPI.swift` (scrapeURL, \
getScrapeStatus, testConnection, listMealPlans, createMealPlan, \
deleteMealPlan) repeats the same ~15 lines: `guard let baseURL` → `guard let \
token` → `URL(string: ...)` → build `URLRequest` → set `Authorization` + \
Content-Type → `applyAccessHeaders` → `urlSession.data` → cast \
`HTTPURLResponse` → status-code branch → `parseError`. Extract a private \
`request<T: Decodable>(method:path:body:)` helper that throws typed errors so \
new endpoints are one-liners. Many of the endpoints exist solely because the \
generated OpenAPI client doesn't cover them yet — the real fix is \
regenerating, but until then a helper would cut ~200 lines.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
  ],
